From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: parenthesize P32 publication check

Make the CPU-range and error test explicit in the dormant P32 publication
guard so the compiler cannot infer an unintended precedence relationship.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not
submission-ready.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
@@ -174,5 +174,5 @@ int mt6797_a72_membership_publish_p32(unsigned int cpu,
 	int ret = -EPERM;
 
-	if (cpu != 8 && cpu != 9 || !error)
+	if ((cpu != 8 && cpu != 9) || !error)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
--
2.50.1
